2001's the fast and the furious found  major success by all accounts and in the  years since  the franchise's spawn has more than left  its mark on hollywood  it has made several big screen stars  taking in both loads of money  over six billion dollars in fact and  made front page news on more than one  occasion  one of the strongest examples of this  phenomenon is the bitter feud between  two of the series biggest names  vin diesel and dwayne the rock johnson  it took hold of the media several years  ago  and seemingly re-emerged on the road to  the premiere of f9  in an interview with men's health diesel  was asked about his experience working  with johnson in previous fast and  furious installments  more specifically he discussed the part  he played in influencing johnson's  performance as luke hobbs  diesel said noting that he went the  extra mile to make hobbs come off as an  in-your-face hard-hitting character  and that he's proud of the final product  my approach at the time was a lot of  tough love to assist in getting that  performance  where it needed to be i would do  anything i'd have to do in order to get  performances in anything i'm producing  at first glance this may just sound like  vin diesel explaining an unorthodox  method to get dwayne johnson's portrayal  of luke hobbs just right  but when you consider their personal  history and various reports from their  time  working on fast and furious films  together diesel's 2021 statement is  completely recontextualized  buckle up let's ride through their rocky  relationship  this story begins on august 8th 2016  when johnson made a since-deleted  instagram post to voices displeasure  with someone on the face of the furious  set  he altered an unnamed person for acting  unprofessional  and not backing up their behavior  clarifying that he was on good terms  with most of the cast and crew otherwise  he wrote when you watch this movie next  april and it seems like i'm not acting  in some of these scenes and my blood is  legit boiling  you're right naturally this opened up  speculation over who he's referring to  even more naturally various news outlets  ran with this developing story and  spread the common belief that vin diesel  was the person johnson was not so subtly  pointing the finger at according to tmz  the two parties met up for a secret  meeting  on august 9 2016 in hopes of putting  their anger to rest  adding that the fate of the furious cast  was unhappy with johnson for causing a  stir at the tail end of the chute  apparently the clash stemmed from  diesel's position as a producer  and is penchant for making changes that  drew the ire of his coaster  later an anonymous source close to the  project told people that the tension  between the actors had been on the rise  for months  a common complaint was johnson's  apparent lack of punctuality  sometimes not appearing at all and  stalling production this angered diesel  but he was far from absolved of any  wrongdoing  other reports claimed he would engage in  similar behavior even locking himself in  his trailer during the filming of  furious 7.  as word of the budding rivalry began to  spread johnson hopped back on instagram  to try and quell any further rumors  about him  diesel or anyone else connected to the  fast and furious name  once again addressing the onset  animosity but highlighting that the  ability to work past it  is what really matters and like with any  team that's a family there's going to be  conflicts  family is going to have differences of  opinion and fundamental core beliefs  to me conflict can be a good thing when  it's followed by great resolution  come august 19th vin diesel took to  facebook to speak directly on the  subject  showing his appreciation for the fans  for their support and letting them know  that  without you i would not be doing fast  date he then detailed their involvement  in johnson landing the hob's role to  begin with  revealing we gave the role that was  originally written for tommy lee jones  we gave it to dwayne and he shined in it  it seems all that sunny chatter didn't  make it all the way to johnson  he made a post of his own that same day  on instagram he announced it wrapped up  on the fate of the furious with a  caption thanking numerous people  involved in making the project a reality  guess who he didn't mention  yup vin diesel though few doubted  johnson and diesel weren't at odds their  fellow  fate of the furious star michelle  rodriguez set the record straight she  told people in september 2016  any human being who knows what men are  like knows to stay out of those  situations  and let them figure it out nevertheless  she clarified that the two were friends  even in the face of their heated  conflict  and would put aside their differences  sooner rather than later  months later the press tour for face of  the furious was in full swing  and diesel expressed his love and  appreciation for johnson  he told usa today on april 7th 2017  i don't think the world really realizes  how close we are in a weird way in my  house he's uncle dwayne  two days later on entertainment tonight  johnson posited that his issues with  diesel boiled down to different  philosophies  and that the most important thing about  juncture was the film itself  with that tmc reported on april 18th  that the two were once again  on good terms and that their beef was  officially squashed  with all of this backstory in mind could  vin diesel's most recent quip about the  rock and his acting abilities reopen old  wounds  you can bet that johnson's cooking up a  response for sure we can practically  smell it now  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  acting rivals are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

